# Vendored STEP corpora are byte-identical to the distributions they came from, and
# THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md says so for the third-party ones. Windows runners default to
# core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite these ASCII files on checkout and make that claim
# false. It applies to the first-party fixture under tests/corpus/gramel too, which is pinned
# by exact rung diameters rather than by counts.
*.stp -text
*.step -text
# Keep these public inputs byte-identical; Git's textual whitespace check would
# otherwise flag the STEP writer's legal trailing spaces on thousands of lines.
tests/corpus/cadgenbench_inputs/*.step -diff
tests/corpus/ttt_inputs/*.step -diff
